Nyaya's source code (mcp/, chat/, web/) is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. Ingested and dual-published legal datasets retain the licenses
and statutory permissions of their respective upstream sources, tracked per
record in `provenance` (`license_spdx`, `commercial_safe`, `terms_status`).

1. Primary Legal Data & Statutory Basis (India)
   - Indian Copyright Act, 1957, Section 52(1)(q)
     * Section 52(1)(q)(ii): Acts of Legislature, Rules, and Regulations.
     * Section 52(1)(q)(iv): Judgments and orders of Courts, Tribunals, and
       other judicial authorities.
   - Eastern Book Company & Ors. v. D.B. Modak & Anr., (2008) 1 SCC 1
     Primary judicial text is reproducible under s. 52(1)(q)(iv); commercial
     reporter editorial headnotes, paragraph numbering, and digests remain
     copyrighted and are strictly excluded from Nyaya.
   - Statutory Non-Publication Exclusions
     Sealed, in-camera, and identity-protected orders (including IPC s. 228A /
     BNS s. 72, POCSO Act ss. 23 & 33(7), Juvenile Justice Act s. 74, and
     HIV/AIDS Act s. 34) are excluded from publication and indexing.

